-- DC item names recovered from shared appearances, generated 2026-08-25.
-- 21474 item_template rows carry the placeholder name 'Item <entry>'. Those entries exist in
-- retail Item.db2 but have NO ItemSparse row (verified: their IDs are single holes between
-- present neighbours, so it is not an extract gap) -- they are appearance-only records and
-- genuinely have no display name of their own.
-- RECOVERY: ItemModifiedAppearance links each to an ItemAppearanceID; a NAMED item sharing
-- that appearance donates its name. That is the right semantic for a wardrobe, where the
-- entry IS the appearance. Where several named siblings exist, the most common name wins
-- (ties alphabetical, so the output is deterministic).
-- Guarded on the placeholder text: idempotent, and cannot overwrite a real name.
-- NOTE: the client caches item data in WDB. After applying, bump version.cache_id (or clear
-- the Cache folder) or clients will keep showing the old placeholder.

